{"id":"6cd8ac9e1db76366","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-prop-rademacher.md","title":"Rademacher Functions","display":"prop-rademacher — Rademacher Functions","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-rademacher","aliases":["58-prop-rademacher"],"display":"prop-rademacher — Rademacher Functions","depends_on":["[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-orthonormal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-rademacher"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-rademacher</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-rademacher — Rademacher Functions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"633f67d630a481ae\" href=\"?note=633f67d630a481ae\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-orthonormal.md\">../batch04/58-df-orthonormal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega=[0,1)\">\\(\\Omega=[0,1)\\)</span> with normalized Lebesgue measure <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r_n(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor-2\\lfloor2^nt\\rfloor}\">\\(r_n(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor-2\\lfloor2^nt\\rfloor}\\)</span> for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n&lt;\\omega\">\\(n&lt;\\omega\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t\\in\\Omega\">\\(t\\in\\Omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta_{mn}\">\\(\\delta_{mn}\\)</span> (Kronecker delta)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\n\\left[\n\\forall F\\in[\\omega]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\forall\\varepsilon:F\\to\\{-1,1\\}\\;\n\\lambda\\bigl(\\{t\\in\\Omega\\mid\n\\forall n\\in F\\;r_n(t)=\\varepsilon(n)\\}\\bigr)=2^{-|F|}\n\\right]\n\\land\n\\left[\n\\forall m,n&lt;\\omega\\;\n\\int_\\Omega r_m(t)r_n(t)\\,d\\lambda(t)=\\delta_{mn}\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\n\\left[\n\\forall F\\in[\\omega]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\forall\\varepsilon:F\\to\\{-1,1\\}\\;\n\\lambda\\bigl(\\{t\\in\\Omega\\mid\n\\forall n\\in F\\;r_n(t)=\\varepsilon(n)\\}\\bigr)=2^{-|F|}\n\\right]\n\\land\n\\left[\n\\forall m,n&lt;\\omega\\;\n\\int_\\Omega r_m(t)r_n(t)\\,d\\lambda(t)=\\delta_{mn}\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The finite joint-distribution formula states mutual independence and implies the symmetric marginal law.</li>\n<li>The Rademacher system is orthonormal but not complete in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^2([0,1),\\lambda)\">\\(L^2([0,1),\\lambda)\\)</span>, so it is not a basis of that space.</li>\n<li>Khinchine's inequality controls norms of finite Rademacher sums.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-integral.md","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-orthonormal.md","status":"resolved","id":"633f67d630a481ae","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-orthonormal.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Omega=[0,1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"r_n(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor-2\\lfloor2^nt\\rfloor}","display":false},{"tex":"n<\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"t\\in\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta_{mn}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}rademacher}\\vdash\n\\left[\n\\forall F\\in[\\omega]^{<\\omega}\\;\n\\forall\\varepsilon:F\\to\\{-1,1\\}\\;\n\\lambda\\bigl(\\{t\\in\\Omega\\mid\n\\forall n\\in F\\;r_n(t)=\\varepsilon(n)\\}\\bigr)=2^{-|F|}\n\\right]\n\\land\n\\left[\n\\forall m,n<\\omega\\;\n\\int_\\Omega r_m(t)r_n(t)\\,d\\lambda(t)=\\delta_{mn}\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"L^2([0,1),\\lambda)","display":false}],"bytes":1195,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3987","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-prop-rademacher.md|58-prop-rademacher]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["68427bc628af9b8d","4884f45058a56aac","633f67d630a481ae"]}